# Expected failures of mortar (spec/harness.md "Markers"), two forms:
#
#   mortar,<arch>: <reason>
#     run-wide: mortar has no back end there yet, so every mortar link of
#     the architecture is expected to fail.
#   mortar[,<arch>...] <test>.test: <reason>
#     one test (its path under tests/link), on the architectures named
#     (all, when none is): the package that makes it pass, "M2: WP-0xx".
#
# A line takes the place of a test's own xfail(mortar) on that
# architecture (a test's skip still applies; a test may not carry both).
# A mortar link that passes is XPASS, so a line goes when its package
# lands: deleting a package's lines is all it takes.

# Run-wide: none (i386 joined with WP-030c).

# M2 (dynamic executables, spec/dyn.md section 16): none; every M2
# package has landed (the last, WP-052 static-pie).

# WP-152: the verifier's mirror of the option table (mortar_plumb
# opts.rs) does not know the rows WP-152 opened, so every mortar link
# that spells one is judged M9 (and only M9: every other rule passes,
# all links checked by the package). The supervisor regenerates the
# mirror at the merge and deletes these lines with it.
mortar resolve/whole-archive.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/whole-archive-defs.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar,aarch64 resolve/whole-archive-debug.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/undefined-root.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/require-defined.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/allow-multiple-definition.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/start-lib.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar,aarch64,x86_64 dyn/shared/whole-archive-shared.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
mortar resolve/whole-archive-members.test: M9 until the WP-152 rows are mirrored
